WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.110
John: Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday!

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.040
Today's video contains many updates about
sports and art which are supposed to be opposites,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.360
but as we shall see today, that dichotomy
- like so many dichotomies - is a lie.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.280
Also for reasons that will soon become clear
I have to wear a lot of shirts today.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.299
So Hank as previously noted, I am auctioning
off my support in the World Cup this year,

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:18.970
which is why I recently acquired gear from
all 32 nations participating in the tournament.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:23.119
Basically if you go to the link in the dooblydoo
you can essentially purchase my love on behalf

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:24.410
of the country of your choice.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:28.840
AND your donation will be 100% tax-deductible,
provided that you live in the United States

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.349
- this isn't seriously our uniform, is it?

00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:34.020
I don't feel like I'm about to play World
Class soccer; I feel like a six-year-old dressed

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.250
for Thanksgiving dinner.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.690
So to date this crazy plan has raised nearly
$6,000 for Nerdfighteria's charity, the Foundation

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.290
to Decrease Worldsuck, but starting today,
all proceeds are going to benefit sarcoma

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.290
research.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.670
Sarcoma is the kind of cancer that Augustus
Waters has in The Fault in Our Stars.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:51.789
It’s also a cancer that lots of actual people
have in real life and it sucks and I hate

00:00:51.789 --> 00:00:53.750
it, so we’re gonna raise some money to fight
sarcoma.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.890
Here’s the deal: every time you donate one
dollar, I will donate three, so your dollar

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.899
is essentially worth four dollars AND I will
support the team of your choice in the World

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:04.970
Cup and I will be the most committed fan in
the world!

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.640
Unless someone else pays me more.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.430
Like Hank, as it stands I’ll be supporting
the Ivory Coast when they play Columbia, and

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:13.000
to prepare myself I have already learned several
songs about Kolo Touré.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.510
[singing] Kolo!

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.960
KOLO KOLO- right no singing.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.250
Okay but maybe you like your soccer slightly
less professional!

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.009
Hank, remember how Nerdfighteria uses advertising
proceeds from a FIFA video series to sponsor

00:01:22.009 --> 00:01:25.630
an actual professional football team that
fights homophobia and racism and is owned

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.630
by its fans?

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.590
Right, well Nerdfightaria-sponsored AFC Wimbledon
finished this season in 20TH, avoiding relegation

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.760
from the fourth tier of English football-
HUZZAH!

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.960
Meanwhile, the fictional AFC Wimbledon Wimbly
Womblys, led by Bald John Green, Other John

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.299
Green, Seb Brown, and Yayayabamba are putting
together a great season!

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:45.009
Hank, I suddenly realized how weird this must
all sound to new nerdfighters, and also to

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:47.350
old nerdfighters, really just to anyone, come
to think of it.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.690
I mean the movie version of my book is coming
out in ten days, and I spend most of my free

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:54.509
time worrying about the health and well-being
of FIFA 14 players who are technically made

00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:55.899
out of 1’s and 0’s.

00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:57.500
Although to be fair, so is the movie.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.909
Okay maybe you like games but you don’t
like soccer, by the way I think this is Argentina,

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:02.219
but it doesn’t show up well in this light.

00:02:02.219 --> 00:02:06.330
Anyway, did you know that there’s an amazing
nerdfighter Minecraft server called Nerdcrafteria

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.330
that also raises money to decrease worldsuck?

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.330
Check it out!

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.050
And now, at last – let’s move on to art.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.040
So Sarah’s new show The Art Assignment is
going great; there’s a new assignment up

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.500
from the brilliant and fascinating artist
Kate Gilmore.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.530
And if you like talking about and/or making
art, you will find a thriving community over

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:24.220
at The Art Assignment, where people are making
everything from, like, gifs to sculptures.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.540
What else is going on?

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:30.380
Oh right, that Nerdfighter Kiva group, that
band of suck decreasers, is very, very close

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:34.270
to 4 million dollars in total loans to entrepreneurs
in the developing world.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.930
So in case you don’t know about Kiva – you
choose a business person to support, you can

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.230
make a loan for as little as $25, and then
they pay you back over time.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.790
And if you’ve never tried it before, your
first loan is free.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:47.010
It’s hard to believe we’ve almost made
4 million dollars in loans.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:50.700
And of course Hank, there’s also SciShow
Space, which has a great community of space

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.160
nerds thinking and talking about our big and
beautiful and terrifying universe.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:59.150
And lastly Nerfighteria’s new community
ambassador Valerie2776 has created an amazing

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.020
map and calendar of upcoming events and gatherings.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.470
Do you have a point, John?

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.720
Yes, I have two points!

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.350
First, look how many shirts I can wear in
a single video!

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:12.771
Secondly, even within the tiny world of Nerdfightaria,
there are lots of ways to connect, via nerdfighter

00:03:12.771 --> 00:03:16.830
gatherings, or if you love art, via The Art
Assignment, or if you love terrible FIFA playing,

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:17.870
via the Wimbly Womblys.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.120
But Hank, at least for me, the best connections
aren’t just about feeling less alone; they’re

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.800
about finding ways to look at the universe
more broadly and enthusiastically.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.330
Whether it’s contemporary art that takes
you there, or soccer, or building worlds in

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:32.170
Minecraft, or learning about space, or working
with entrepreneurs around the world, or whatever,

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.040
it’s great to feel alive to the world.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.750
For me it’s less about what you like than
it is about how you like it.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.050
Like, I’m not a huge fan of boxing, but
the poet Richard Katrovas is, and he once

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:46.670
wrote that to him, boxing serves "as a mottled
lens / Unto the bifurcated human heart / Whose

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.020
one true nature is to break apart."

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.720
Hank, I'd like to think that the human heart
has more than one true nature, but regardless,

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.820
here’s my question for you, nerdfighters
– what’s your lens these days?

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:55.820
I did it!

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.520
I wore all 32 shirts in a video!

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.520
Via Brasil!

00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.900
Hank, I will see you on Friday.

